<font color="#993322">

<table align='CENTER' cellpadding='2' border='1' cellspacing='2' background='http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif'><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?month=12">This Month</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?month=11">November-2001</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?month=10">October-2001</A></TD></TR><TR><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?month=9">September-2001</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?month=8">August-2001</A></TD><TD><a HREF="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/newspages/news.php?month=7">July-2001</A></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Legerdemain Cook-Out!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - September 22nd 2001</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif" cellpadding="5" border="0" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'>Had a ball at Legerdemain's second guild cook-out!!<BR>
In the lower level range, we had some one-on-one competitions.  Keymara won out over Torpor, and Gisstarak edged in victory over MrVegas.  Zarana barely lost to Gisstarak after that, and finally, Gisstarak  got the killing blow againts Keymara.to win the competition.<BR>
A lot of equipment and items were exchanged in-between the events, while several loving guildmembers beat the holy tar out of eachother hehe.<BR>
The higher level range sported a team event.  Team one consisted of Zzeep, Celly, Futtal, Terrenoth, Kennington and Sagera.  Team two had Keymarad, Fumbles, Wende, Mythilk, Kiglan and Roldanoius.  We had a great time taunting eachother before the fight while waiting for Koldwind to return from LD hehe.  Unfortunately, Koldwind was unable to get back in time and the competition continued.  It seems that Team Two picked Terrenoth as their main target and eliminated me quickly hehe.  Team one got several good hits in on kiglan and would have killed a few of Team Two's members, but for the healing hands of Keymarad Tigerpaw.  It was a valient struggle, but Team Two took the pize.<BR>
The next event was our famous Nekkid Drunk Race hehe.  After everyone was ... swaying in the breeze so-to-speak.. and three sheets to the wind... heheh... they ran around the arena and back again picking up a couple tokens along the way.  The only thing that woul have made this competition more hilarious would have been the ability to spread vegtable oil along the arena's floors :><BR>
In order of their success... Kiglan, Mythilk, Roldanious, Celly, Fumbles, Zarana, Sagera, and Wende completed the trek without breaking any bones.<BR>
See ya'll there next time! :></font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font face='monotype sorts' size='+1'>) </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Kaesora Raid!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - September 16th 2001</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif" cellpadding="5" border="0" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'><p class='text'>Kaesora provided a terrific dungeon for our lower level raid.  Again we had two groups of 25ish to 35ish characters.  Two brand new members also joined us on this event.  They were freshly invited under Orlo's sponsorship.</p>
<p class='text'>Kaesora is great for several reasons; the exp bonus, tanks can be bound right outside, and it's never packed.  Unfortunately, it's a little far away from a bank or training hall for most.  Also, killing mobs in Kaesora will give you bad Venril Sathir faction.</p>
<p class='text'>We ended up bagging Xalog.  He downed one of our groups in the process, but we got him! hehe. Junenita was awarded the Fang of Xalog.  I hope she'll eventually use it to get her Howling Stones key.</p></font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font face='monotype sorts' size='+1'>) </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Plane of Fear with HOS</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Friday - September 14th 2001</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif" cellpadding="5" border="0" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'><p class='text'>A few Legerdemain members joined <A HREF='http://www.harmonyofsouls.org'>Harmony of Souls</A> in the Plane of Fear.  Embren and Keymarad had camped up there the day before to help ease the break-in.  Bonecaster was kind enough to run the whole thing and everything went great.  Orlo, Celly, Roldanious, and Tienen(run by skrambold) joined in the festivities as the evening progressed.</P>
<p class='text>There was only one small misshap near the end of the raid which caused a .. little.. massacre hehe.  After we were all Rezzed we called it a night.  I had a great time considering it was my first time in Fear.  Definatly something I'd do again.</p></font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font face='monotype sorts' size='+1'>) </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Epic Fight!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Friday - September 14th 2001</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif" cellpadding="5" border="0" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'><p class='text'>Wende was awarded her Earthstained Note as part of her epic quest.  Roldanious gathered several members in East Karana for the fight.  From what I hear, the fight went smoothly and quickly.  I don't have all the names of those who attended, but gratz to Wende!! :>
</p></font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font face='monotype sorts' size='+1'>) </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Droga Raid!</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Sunday - September 9th 2001</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif" cellpadding="5" border="0" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'><p class='text'>We decided to raid Droga for this Sunday's lower level raid.  We eventually gathered two low level groups together for the fun.  Most of the people playing were alternate characters, but we still had plenty of fun hehe.  We didn't go in very far.  We found a large room and settled in for a few hours.  There was constant mob pulling and we were in no hurry to rush off somewhere else.</P>
<p class='text'>This was the first Raid type event for a couple of the attenders.  With a little more experience, I hope we can come back to Droga and adventure around a little more.  Good work gang! :></P></font><BR><font size='-2' face='arial'>------submitted by </font><font face='monotype sorts' size='+1'>) </font><font size='-1' face='arial'><a href=mailto:Terrenoth@yahoo.com>Terrenoth</a></font></TD></TR></TABLE><BR><TABLE align="center" width="85%" border="0"  margin="0" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0"><TR><TD ALIGN="center"><IMG SRC="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/La.jpg"></TD><TD width="40%" VALIGN="center" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<font face='Impact'>Hate Raid</font></TD><TD VALIGN="center" ALIGN="right" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif"><font size='-1' face='Georgia'>Saturday - September 1st 2001</font>&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</TD></TR></TABLE><TABLE width="85%" align="CENTER" background="http://www.Guild-Legerdemain.com/images/texture3.gif" cellpadding="5" border="0" margin="0" cellspacing="0"><TR><TD><font face='comic sans ms'><p>
Contratulations on our first hate raid!!!  It didn't start out extreemly well, but we eventually got things moving in a posative direction.  The initial strategy was to fight at the zone-in to begin with and then either move toward the Safe Spot or toward the Thone room.  That didn't work out as well as I would have liked.  We were killing the mobs just fine, but a Spite Golem got the best of us.  Since we couldn't get it snared, it ran off and alerted all kinds of nearby friends that we were visiting.
</p>
<p>
Eventually, we moved the corpses and the raid over to the Safe Spot since one particular Spite Golem was on the patrol route and wasn't gonna leave us alone.  We had a few people trade in and out of groups and we continued to hunt.  It took quite a long time, but I believe was very successful considering it was the first time in hate for a great deal of the participants.
</p>
